# Dev / test
tests/
docs/
# Prose is excluded because it is not needed at run time -- with two exceptions
# the image cannot start without. CONSTITUTION.md is copied by the Dockerfile and
# core/constitution.py verifies it against a SHA-256 pin on every boot, so
# excluding it made the build fail at `COPY pyproject.toml CONSTITUTION.md`
# rather than merely producing a slimmer image. The pin is the point of the
# constitution: an image that ships without the file it verifies cannot enforce
# it, and silently skipping the check is exactly the failure mode the pin
# exists to prevent.
*.md
!README.md
!CONSTITUTION.md

# Dev config
.env.example
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.cursorrules
TAG

# Docker self
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
